# Cloudflare Workers + Pages (Static Assets) response-header rules.
#
# Wrangler doesn't expose response headers from `wrangler.jsonc`
# directly — the canonical surface is a `_headers` file copied into
# the assets directory at build time. Vite picks this file up from
# `web/public/` and emits it to `web/dist/_headers`; Cloudflare's
# Static Assets runtime serves it.
#
# Syntax (one rule block per path glob, `/*` matches every route):
#   /pattern
#     Header-Name: value
#
# Content Security Policy
# -----------------------
# The SPA serves no inline <script>; our own code all goes through
# Vite's bundled module graph, so `script-src 'self'` covers it.
# `https://static.cloudflareinsights.com` is the one external script
# the app loads: the Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon (beacon.min.js).
# We don't ship the beacon <script> ourselves — Cloudflare injects it
# at the edge (Web Analytics "Enable" / automatic injection) into the
# served HTML. But the browser still enforces CSP against the injected
# tag, so `static.cloudflareinsights.com` (script) and
# `cloudflareinsights.com` (the RUM POST, see connect-src) must be
# allow-listed here regardless of who injects the tag. The beacon is
# privacy-first and cookieless.
#
# `style-src 'self'`: Vite's production build emits all CSS as
# external `<link rel="stylesheet">` assets — there are no inline
# `<style>` blocks in `dist/index.html`. Dev mode (HMR) uses inline
# styles, but `_headers` only applies on Cloudflare, so that's not a
# real constraint. If a future plugin starts inlining critical CSS,
# add `'unsafe-inline'` back with a one-line justification.
#
# `font-src 'self'`: all four families ship via
# `@fontsource-variable/*` and are bundled with the build. No
# external font requests on any page.
#
# `img-src 'self' data:`: SVG icons inlined as data: URIs.
#
# `connect-src 'self' https://api.urbanistatlas.com https://cloudflareinsights.com`:
# outbound fetches go to the Atlas API plus `cloudflareinsights.com`,
# where the Web Analytics beacon POSTs its cookieless RUM data.
#
# `frame-ancestors 'none'`: nobody embeds the Atlas in an iframe.
#
# Other headers
# -------------
# `Strict-Transport-Security`: opt into HSTS with a one-year
# max-age + subdomain coverage. Cloudflare terminates TLS in front
# of us, so HTTPS is already enforced at the edge — the header is
# defense in depth for clients that handle the upgrade themselves.
#
# `Permissions-Policy`: turn off browser features the Atlas has no
# legitimate reason to touch. `frame-ancestors 'none'` already
# stops embedding, but explicit feature opt-out is cheap insurance.
#
# Adjust this file when adding a new origin (e.g. a future analytics
# endpoint) — and document the change in `docs/deploy.md`.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://api.urbanistatlas.com https://cloudflareinsights.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
